## Strategy: EMA(5/15/60) Pullback-to-EMA60

Three-EMA stack trend filter with pullback entry to the slowest EMA.

Source: Thomas Carter, 20 Forex Trading Strategies (1 Hour Time Frame), 2014. URL: local PDF archive.

Target symbols: EURUSD.DWX, GBPUSD.DWX. Timeframe: H1.

Expected trade frequency: H1 EMA-stack pullbacks to EMA60 are recurring trend-continuation setups; conservatively about 24 trades per year per symbol.

### Setup

**Bull**: EMA5 > EMA15 > EMA60, both EMA60 and EMA15 sloping upward.  
**Bear**: EMA5 < EMA15 < EMA60, both sloping downward.

### Entry

Wait for price to pull back and touch (or come within 1-2 pips of) EMA60.  
Enter Long (bull) or Short (bear) at market on the touch.

### Exit

- **SL**: 30 pips from entry
- **TP**: 50 pips from entry (R:R ≈ 1.67)

### Notes

No re-entry if stop is hit. If EMA stack breaks during the pullback (EMA5 crosses EMA15), the setup is invalidated — skip the trade.
